The first executable check found a subtle serialization detail worth catching: the source-row training label and the exact rational extension differ by a few binary64 rounding bits on some rows, even though both represent the exact-path target. I’m tightening the verifier to require a quantified numerical residual against the rational target, while still using byte equality for the surrogate-fallback test. This is exactly the distinction the provenance gate needs.
