+**The exact source/C3 intersection is 22 anchors; the stated 6,000-label random sample matches the sealed surrogate fallback on 359/6,000 labels (5.9833%); exact-versus-surrogate argmax disagreement is C1 1,137/2,200 (51.6818%), C2 1,216/2,200 (55.2727%), and C3 18/22 (81.8182%); the declared converged run did not launch because the mandated runner rejects its 4,000-update schedule.**
+
+# EXACT corpus assembly and training preflight — 2026-09-10
+
+`BUILD_NOT_CLAIM`. No EE quantity was computed. Loss values were not used as evidence about EE.
+
+## Outcome
+
+The exact-label corpus was assembled at
+`/home/sat/mcrl-v025-exacttrain-ws/artifacts/exact-label-corpus-20260910`.
+It contains 22 exact source-view shards and 22 exact C3 coalition shards, plus
+their 44 SHA-256 sidecars. The unchanged production reader accepted 21,532
+source rows and 4,552 coalition rows with corpus digest
+`3dd10c17409789b945185ba435d3159052c11d36933158fc7958ae11b5a108e9`.
+
+Parts 1 and 2 pass. The Part 3 production launch was stopped before an output
+directory was created: the required runner, SHA-256
+`4885570b8552dc95a2143764cc10bd7b78f06504d63c4fa07866817bfc797d66`,
+accepts only 1–2,000 epochs and implements the legacy constant-rate,
+exact-budget/no-early-selection contract. It cannot express the declared
+4,000-update step decay and cadence-100 stability stopping rule without
+changing the sealed implementation or inventing a new runner and held-out
+split.
+
+## Part 1 — exact anchor intersection
+
+Verified by running code: the exact source corpus has 93 admitted prefix
+anchors and the exact C3 build has 22 anchors. Their intersection is the 22
+development anchors below. No post-deadline quarantined anchor and no
+evaluation-only date was read.
+
+- `global-000`: `V025_PROBE/world/1|step=0|carrier=nearest-eligible`
